# 🌍 The Reality Layer

Atlas does not treat reality as an abstract database.

It treats reality as the laboratory.

The system may ingest signals from:

```text
People
Sensors
Satellites
GIS
Drones
Phones
Machines
Vehicles
Cameras
Industrial systems
Enterprise systems
Scientific instruments
Open datasets
Human observations
Field research
```

These signals can describe:

* cities
* farms
* supply chains
* hospitals
* factories
* roads
* energy systems
* water networks
* markets
* ecosystems
* infrastructure
* communities
* environmental conditions

The objective is not surveillance for its own sake.

The objective is **better understanding of systems so that people can make better decisions**.

---

# 🧠 The Atlas Core

At the center of Atlas Sanctum is the **Atlas Core**.

It is envisioned as a living computational system that combines models, graphs, policies, agents, simulations, knowledge, and real-world observations.

### Core capabilities

| Capability                | Purpose                                                    |
| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| Regenerative Intelligence | Optimize toward long-term ecological and social resilience |
| Civilization Intelligence | Understand large-scale human systems                       |
| Moral Intelligence        | Encode ethical constraints and human oversight             |
| Opportunity Graph         | Discover hidden connections between needs and resources    |
| Knowledge Graph           | Organize structured knowledge and relationships            |
| Policy Engine             | Translate principles and rules into executable policies    |
| AI Agents                 | Perform reasoning, planning, research, and execution       |
| Simulation Engine         | Explore possible futures before acting                     |
| Impact Ledger             | Track outcomes and real-world effects                      |
| Trust & Identity          | Establish secure identities and permissions                |
| Economic Coordination     | Connect capital, projects, infrastructure, and outcomes    |

