# 🕸️ Opportunity Graph

One of the central concepts in Atlas is the **Opportunity Graph**.

Instead of looking at a problem in isolation, Atlas models relationships between:

```text
Needs
Resources
People
Skills
Capital
Infrastructure
Knowledge
Problems
Projects
Markets
Ecological Systems
Opportunities
```

This allows hidden relationships to become visible.

### Example

```text
Unused Machinery
       +
Skilled Workers
       +
Waste Materials
       +
Housing Demand
       ↓
Local Manufacturing Opportunity
       ↓
New Enterprise
       ↓
Local Jobs
       ↓
Infrastructure
       ↓
Community Value
```

The graph turns fragmented information into potential action.

