# 🌍 Africa as a Living Laboratory

Atlas can begin where real-world complexity is abundant.

Africa provides environments containing:

* rapidly growing cities
* emerging industries
* distributed communities
* informal economies
* infrastructure gaps
* renewable-energy potential
* agricultural systems
* biodiversity
* ambitious entrepreneurs
* scientific institutions
* manufacturing opportunities
* large-scale coordination challenges

**Nairobi and East Africa can serve as an initial laboratory.**

The architecture, however, is deliberately global.

```text
WORKSHOP
   ↓
COMMUNITY
   ↓
CITY
   ↓
REGION
   ↓
NATION
   ↓
CONTINENT
   ↓
PLANET
```

The ambition is not to build "an African version" of an existing system.

It is to build infrastructure capable of contributing something genuinely new to the world.

